    threshold ∧ meta_shift_ratio high → pause + request reframe from S5)
  constraints: S3_C1 respect S5 hard bounds (crossing cap = double-loop)
    S3_C2 no S4 substitution (no environmental scanning; S3 modules never call Ollama/Qwen)
    S3_C3 params.json atomic write (.tmp + rename; S1 polls at tick boundary)
    S3_C4 trust updates monotonic in policy (decrease on violation, increase only via
      successful ticks or witness attestation — no arbitrary boost)
    S3_C5 audit-readable (every S3 function emits ≥ 1 event)
  invariants: {
    S3_I1 resource conservation (Σ S1 allocations ≤ S5 budget at all times; else refuse + algedonic)
    S3_I2 regulation responsiveness (S1 threshold crossed → S3 acts within 3 ticks)
    S3_I3 S5 policy compliance (zero params.json violations; S3* periodic audit)
    S3_I4 escalation correctness (100% bound-violations escalate — absorption = corruption indicator)
    S3_I5 trust composition integrity (every delta has justifying event; D11/D11b)
  }
  impl: cgroup.rs ✓ | telemetry_publisher.rs ◐ (publishes, doesn't yet consume)
    | s4_operational.rs::publish_s4_analysis ✓ | params.json writer ✗ | trust D11 ◐ | escalation ✗
  llm: L=2 CAN use, but "kernel first" — deterministic math + rule-based; delegates cognitive
    to S4; LLM role limited to audit explanations + rare policy revision proposals to S5
  confidence: identity ✓ interface ✓ decisions ◐ constraints ✓ invariants ◐
}

s3star_audit = {
  identity: ANTI-CAPTURE channel — sporadic, direct (reads S1 events.jsonl sans S3 mediation),
    asymmetric (reports to S5 ONLY; S3 cannot intercept). Mandatory: Cybersyn 1973 — Opsroom
    destroyed because no S3*-like mechanism.
  // maps to: covenant hash verify at boot, honeypot (COVENANT_MISMATCH), external witnesses,
