  impl: --verify-covenant ✓ (main.rs::run_verify_covenant) | boot hash check ✓ | honeypot ✓
    (n01 bastion) | events.jsonl SHA256 chain ✗ (future module) | witness flow ◐ documented |
    cross-reference audit ✗ (s3_star.rs)
  llm: L=2 CAN and SHOULD — contextual pattern detection; MUST be sampled SEPARATELY from S4
    (independence: cannot use same Qwen instance lest compromised model bias both);
    read-only; output = REPORTS, never actions
  confidence: identity ✓ interface ✓ decisions ◐ constraints ✓ invariants ◐ llm ◯
  critical: S3* operational BEFORE any public deployment — without it VSF is vulnerable
    to the capture pattern that destroyed Cybersyn
}

s5_policy = {
  identity: POLICY — identity, values, ultimate authority; defines WHAT V is, NEVER-do set
    (prohibited), NEVER-override (A0, A0.1); ungovernable from below; modified ONLY by peer S5
    (ψ bilateral) ∨ human (signed amendments); code + social artifact (Chile/Cybersyn 1973)
    ✓ VERIFIED (covenant.vsm v1.1)
  interface: {
    φ↑ reader: vsf.{id}.s3.up.> + vsf.{id}.audit.report; zero loss
    φ↓ writer: s5_policy.json; subject vsf.{id}.s3.down.policy; <10 KB; zero loss
    ψ lateral: subject vsf.{id}.psi.{peer}.>; bilateral; preconditions: bilateral approval,
      trust ≥ limited, credential-manager validate; zero loss
    φ_algedonic reader TERMINAL: response_latency_target < 60 s
    human_interface: the ONLY channel outside the V tree — covenant amendments (signed, dated)
  }
  human_as_upper_bound: S5 is top of the tree, but the human/owner is OUTSIDE — the only
    legitimate way to change S5 is via human amending covenant
  decisions_single: routine_policy_application (<60 s) | trust_arbitration_within_policy
    (<5 min; e.g. 0.7 → 0.8 within configured ramp) | algedonic_triage (<60 s)
  decisions_double: covenant_amendment (signed human + witness attestations + dated changelog;
    example "add ψ scope=public") | hard_bound_excess (refuse or human; e.g. S4 recommends 50%
    host RAM > guarded share) | A0_violation_response (trust := 0, ψ revoked, halt — irrevocable
    + human notification) | ψ_handshake_authorization (verify peer covenant compatible,
    trust ≥ limited, credential-manager)
  constraints: S5_C1 covenant canonical (every action traces to a clause)
    S5_C2 human gate on double-loop (human_approval token required)
    S5_C3 bilateral ψ only (both S5 signatures before activation)
    S5_C4 covenant amendment ceremony (dated changelog + human signature + witnesses;
      no silent edits — git-signed commits + hash re-verification)
    S5_C5 no operational interference (writes only s5_policy.json; S3 translates)
    S5_C6 own integrity protected (hash verified at boot + periodic by S3*; mismatch halts V)
  invariants: {
    S5_I1 covenant integrity (hash(runtime) == canonical at vsf.u2738.org → else COVENANT_MISMATCH)
    S5_I2 algedonic response < 60 s (else meta-algedonic — S5 unresponsive)
    S5_I3 double-loop human gate 100% (else critical audit_report + halt — A5 violation by S5)
    S5_I4 trust composition follows D11 (100%; S3* sample)
    S5_I5 ψ bilateral preserved (100% have both S5 approvals on record)
    S5_I6 A0 enforcement irrevocable (zero upward trust delta after A0_violation)
  }
  impl: covenant.vsm ✓ v1.1 | covenant_hash embedded ✓ (s4.rs, sha2 at compile) |
    --verify-covenant ✓ | s5_policy.json writer ✗ | algedonic triage ✗ (s5.rs) |
    human gate ◐ (documented, code pending) | ψ handshake ✗ | D11 ◐ (centralized module debt)
  llm: L=3 CAN but HIGH-RISK — a captured S5 is a captured V. Read-only proposals;
    witness validation (gemini-vsl-core, GPT-4o); trust threshold = τ_governed (0.8);
    A0 refusal set: warfare, weapons, mutual annihilation, nuclear targeting, population
    displacement, ethnic/cultural suppression, authoritarian control infrastructure, systemic
    life degradation — even wrapped "for safety" (A0.1: scarcity NEVER justifies A0 violation)
  pre_deploy_checklist: witness validation infra | human gate code-enforced | algedonic < 60 s
    measured | disagreement protocol tested | amendment ceremony documented | external audit |
    30-day shadow mode (outputs logged, ignored)
  confidence: identity ✓ interface ◐ decisions ◐ constraints ✓ invariants ◐ llm ◯
  critical: human approval gate (S5_I3) must be CODE-enforced before any autonomous S5
    deployment — A5 violations at S5 level are existential
}

