      action, scope, rationale, loop_type: "single", llm_source} | double {proposal_type:
      "human_approval_required", loop_type: "double", human_approval_required: true,
      witness_attestation_required: true} | refusal {proposal_type: "A0_refusal",
      violated_axiom: "A0", violation_set_match, evidence, action_taken: "trust := 0 +
      algedonic"}
    validator (s5.rs to implement): JSON schema (3 formats) | covenant clause verification |
      loop classification | human gate BLOCK until token | A0 enforcement immediate (trust=0 +
      algedonic + halt) | witness verification (ψ approvals, amendments) | self-modification check
    witness validation mandatory: random sample → witnesses verify against own covenant copy;
      disagreement protocol (2 witnesses disagree → halt + escalate human); monthly attestation
    deployment gate: LAST agent; pre-deploy checklist (witness infra, human gate code-enforced,
      algedonic < 60 s, disagreement protocol, amendment ceremony, external audit, 30-day
      shadow mode); only then proposals influence operations
}

opsroom = {
  geometry: Cybersyn 7-chair adapted — VSF has 8 chairs: Orchestrator (center) + S5/S4/S3*
    above + S3/S2/S1 below + Research + Guest; operator (human) = final S5 authority above all;
    no agent overrides them; some propose, all explain, the human signs
  seats: Orchestrator (main Claude — decides which specialists to convene, assembles outputs,
    escalates) | S1/S2/S3/S3*/S4/S5 specialists (R&D mirrors of runtime roles) | Research
    (papers, experiments queue, results indexing) | Guest (ad-hoc bounded specialists:
    dashboards, audits, UI)
  uniform file template (8 sections): persona | runtime context | read scope | write scope |
    tools | when to convene | hand-off protocol | escalation
  policy_alignment (inherits runtime hard rules): WSL boundary (edit/draft/audit — NEVER
    cargo build/test/run, NEVER apt, NEVER deploy — builds on n02) | state.db is canon (query
    FIRST; events.jsonl downstream) | deploy path discipline (components.deploy_path, never
    guess; G-D.4 timer alarms ≤5 min on wrong path) | witness verify not recompute
    (vsf-checkpoint-verify) | auditor continuo already runs (vsf-auditd.timer ~1/h Poisson;
    read state.db.audits) | A5 double-loop = human (all specialist outputs are PROPOSALS) |
    single source = orchestrator (arbitrates disputes, presents both views to operator)
  session flow: operator → orchestrator (HANDOFF+memory+state.db) → task NL → solo/convene/guest
    → specialist Agent()(per-system docs) → proposals → assemble + validate invariants
    → operator signs (always, no exception) → commit + state.db → runtime next deploy
  not_D6_violation: runtime S1-S3 = deterministic Rust unchanged; runtime S3*/S4/S5 = Qwen;
    opsroom = Claude in WSL, NOT in runtime loop — guest agents safe by construction
    (commits → git → human review → deploy)
}

